Package: adaptsimex
Type: Package
Title: Adaptive SIMEX for Poisson Regression with Classical Measurement
    Error
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Gaurav", "Garg", email = "ggarg@iiml.ac.in",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ramakrushna", "Mishra", role = "aut"))
Description: Adaptive SIMEX (A-SIMEX) corrects covariate measurement
    error in Poisson regression by simulation extrapolation with
    cross-validated hyperparameters (extrapolation region and polynomial
    degree, one-standard-error parsimony rule), a two-stage ridge
    extrapolation, and an analytic sandwich variance estimator that
    decomposes into data and simulation components. Also provides the
    Nakamura (1990) corrected score and regression calibration
    competitors. Methods and evidence: Garg and Mishra, "Adaptive SIMEX
    for Poisson Regression with Classical Measurement Error".
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: stats, graphics
Suggests: testthat
